    "notes": "<p><strong>The escort car.</strong> Two Knight Errant guards precede Euphoria's Nightsky in this.</p><p><strong>Price note:</strong> this carries the SR2 catalogue's <strong>20,000¥</strong>, not QE's printed 80,000¥ — taking the catalogue entry whole means taking its price. Ruled acceptable 2026-08-03 (\"I don't know that the price really matters in this case\").</p><p><strong>Conversion: p.283 method A.</strong> This vehicle exists in SR2, so the module takes the system catalogue entry whole rather than carrying SR1 numbers across — the same call already made for Craft's Ares Predator. Ruled by futurekill 2026-08-03 for consistency with how every weapon in the module was converted. The ×3 vehicle-armour rule therefore does NOT apply here: the catalogue entry already prints SR2-scale armour, and doing both would double-count.</p><p>The ubiquitous mid-size sedan of the sprawl.</p><p><em>Cruising speed 35 m/CT (used for vehicle tests). Max speed 105 m/CT. Stats: SR2E p.264-265.</em></p><p><em>Stats verified against the Rigger 2 Vehicle List (SR2, book p.148+). Handling 4/8.</em></p>"
